    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d142-a1-a3">

                <pb facs="0259" n="217" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg217"/>

                <head>Lord Russell to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-03-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 27, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of yesterday, calling attention to two vessels, the Phantom and
                    the Southerner, supposed to be destined for the service of the so-called
                    Confederate States, and I have to acquaint you that the proper departments of
                    her Majesty’s government will be requested to make immediate inquiries on the
                    subject.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUSSELL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. F. Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
